    "landing_testimonials_UnjRNd": {
      "type": "landing-testimonials",
      "blocks": {
        "testimonial_kC6Ncc": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "quote": "Gratitude is the #1 result of being filled with the Spirit of God! I pray this book will inspire a flood of thankfulness in your soul. What an important reminder that the abundant source of thanksgiving is the amazing grace of God. The apostle Paul was a man whose life and letters dripped with gratitude. 1 Thessalonians 5:18 embodies the heart of Paul and amplifies the essence of a thankful heart. In Thanks Living, my friend Stu Epperson Jr. gives a clarion call to every believer to live in gratitude fueled by grace. Read it, share it, and live it—to the glory of God.",
            "name": "Dr. David Jeremiah",
            "meta": "Small group leader",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "testimonial_GLBhnN": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "quote": "Having lived many years with pain and disability, I've learned that thanks Living is not the denial of suffering but the doorway to deeper joy in Jesus. In Thanks Living, Stu Epperson warmly points readers to Christ and shows how a grateful heart can flourish even in life's hardest places. This encouraging book will help you offer up thanksgiving as a way of life",
            "name": "Joni Eareckson Tada",
            "meta": "Small group leader",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "testimonial_CNRapa": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "quote": "Thanks Living is like helium to the heart. It lifts your spirits and fills your heart with joy. This is one of the most enjoyable books I've read in some time. Stu provides a solid biblical foundation for a grateful mind, building his message around a single, significant Bible verse and illustrating it with engaging stories and enriching quotations. Once you begin reading this book, you won't want to put it down. I gladly recommend it to you.",
            "name": "Robert J. Morgan",
            "meta": "Small group leader",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "testimonial_kXUUqD": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "quote": "If you allow the message of this book to take root in the soil of your heart, you will find yourself trusting God even in the face of adversity and personal hardship. Drawing on the teaching of scripture and real-life situations, Stu shows us how obeying the command \"in everything give thanks\" actually lifts our burdens, gives us a divine perspective, and honors God. Read this book, let its message transform you, and share it with others.",
            "name": "Dr. Erwin W. Lutzer, Pastor Emeritus",
            "meta": "Small group leader",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "testimonial_ekbYrU": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "quote": "This heartfelt book beautifully illustrates the life-changing power of gratitude. Drawing from scripture, personal stories, and faithful reflection, it invites us to move beyond occasional thankfulness into a daily rhythm of 'thanks living.' It is a compelling reminder that even in life's hardest moments, a grateful heart can transform how we see everything.",
            "name": "Anthony Atala, MD",
            "meta": "Small group leader",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "testimonial_BWymbi": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "quote": "Stu Epperson takes a straightforward verse from Thessalonians and turns it into a practical reminder that Christians are called to give thanks in every season, circumstance, and even through suffering. Gratitude is a form of worship! This book caused me to reflect on the suffering I have witnessed through war, famine, disease, and evil over many years. Stu brings emphasis to a timeless truth: God is in control. He is faithful. We can, and should, always give THANKS.",
            "name": "Ken Isaacs",
            "meta": "Small group leader",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "testimonial_bPkbtJ": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "quote": "Stu Epperson played basketball for me at The Master's University. In Thanks Living, he encourages the reader to spiritually understand the reality of God’s grace in every circumstance. Our team had outstanding achievements, record wins, and conference championships. We lost basketball games when he played for me, but we were never defeated.",
            "name": "Mel Hankinson",
            "meta": "Small group leader",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "testimonial_3zERpY": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "quote": "Some books capture content well, some a writer's personality, and others a timely message. This one does them all. From sensing the author's command of biblical passages to weaving in historic and modern stories, Thanks Living works. I found myself envisioning Stu before his packed Wednesday in the Word sessions at Dairi-O unpacking these passages with ease. It's a delightful and interactive read with enough depth to fill one's soul. Engagingly practical.",
            "name": "Dr. Jerry Pattengale",
            "meta": "Small group leader",
            "rating": 5
          }
        },
        "testimonial_Ckiwwg": {
          "type": "testimonial",
          "settings": {
            "quote": "Gratitude is the #1 result of being filled with the Spirit of God! I pray this book will inspire a flood of thankfulness in your soul. What an important reminder that the abundant source of thanksgiving is the amazing grace of God. The apostle Paul was a man whose life and letters dripped with gratitude. 1 Thessalonians 5:18 embodies the heart of Paul and amplifies the essence of a thankful heart. In Thanks Living, my friend Stu Epperson Jr. gives a clarion call to every believer to live in gratitude fueled by grace. Read it, share it, and live it—to the glory of God",
            "name": "Dr. David Jeremiah",
            "meta": "Small group leader",
            "rating": 5
          }
        }
      },
