    "landing_faq_VwAd67": {
      "type": "landing-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_item_1": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is Thanks Living about?",
            "answer": "<p>Thanks Living by Stu Epperson Jr. is a book about developing a daily life of gratitude rooted in scripture. Through biblical teaching, personal stories, and practical reflection, the book shows how thanksgiving can shape our faith, perspective, relationships, and response to both blessings and difficult circumstances.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_item_2": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does “Thanks Living” mean?",
            "answer": "<p>“Thanks Living” means making gratitude a way of life rather than something practiced only when circumstances are good. It is the practice of recognizing God's faithfulness and choosing thanksgiving in every season of life.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_item_3": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does the Bible say about giving thanks in all circumstances?",
            "answer": "<p>First Thessalonians 5:18 teaches, “In everything give thanks; for this is the will of God in Christ Jesus concerning you.” Thanks Living explores how this biblical principle can become part of everyday life, including during uncertainty, loss, hardship, and seasons of joy.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_item_4": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How can I practice gratitude every day?",
            "answer": "<p>You can practice gratitude through prayer, scripture, remembering God's faithfulness, thanking others, and intentionally recognizing blessings throughout the day. Thanks Living provides biblical encouragement and practical reflection to help make thanksgiving a daily rhythm.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_item_5": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How can I be thankful when life is difficult?",
            "answer": "<p>Being thankful during difficult circumstances does not mean ignoring pain or pretending everything is good. Biblical gratitude helps us remember God's character and faithfulness, maintain hope, and approach difficult seasons with a different perspective.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_item_6": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Who wrote Thanks Living?",
            "answer": "<p>Thanks Living was written by Stu Epperson Jr., a broadcaster, speaker, and ministry leader. Drawing from scripture, personal experiences, ministry experiences, and stories of faith,Stu encourages readers to make gratitude an everyday way of life.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_item_7": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Who wrote the foreword to Thanks Living?",
            "answer": "<p>The foreword to <em>Thanks Living</em> was written by Dr. Gary Chapman, best-selling author of <em>The 5 Love Languages</em> and a renowned speaker and counselor.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_item_8": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Who should read Thanks Living?",
            "answer": "<p>Thanks Living is for anyone who wants to grow in gratitude, strengthen their faith, and develop a more thankful perspective on everyday life. It can be read individually or shared with families, churches, Bible studies, and small groups.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_item_9": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is Thanks Living suitable for Bible studies or small groups?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Thanks Living can be used for personal reading, Bible studies, church groups, families, and small groups. Its combination of scripture, stories, and practical reflection can encourage meaningful conversations about gratitude, faith, hardship, and God's faithfulness.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_item_10": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Where can I buy Thanks Living, and are bulk discounts available?",
            "answer": "<p>Thanks Living is published by Moody Publishers and is available through Moody Publishers and participating book retailers. For bulk purchases, orders of 12 or more eligible books receive a 40% discount when ordered through Moody Publishers, subject to Moody Publishers' current bulk-order terms.</p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        }
      },
